# Next phase: coordinated record review

Requested by the owner on 9 October 2026. Start after the eleven current human reviews are complete.

Coordinator: manage the queue, unique IDs, exact versions, assignments and review history.

Agent 1 — Author: asynchronously draft 50 manual-grounded record IDs with readable conversation turns, citations, conditions, warnings and stopping rules, using the eleven accepted examples as the reference.

Agent 2 — Source reviewer: independently inspect each record against original PDF pages and provide specific corrections, including missed warning scope, prerequisites, unsupported branches and wrong stopping conditions.

Agent 3 — Feedback judge: adjudicate feedback and revised content against the original source and product policy. Return unresolved items to the author/reviewer loop; confirm when the feedback is satisfactorily resolved.

Coordinator closes each successful agent-review loop and advances the queue. Multiple groups may process disjoint records if concurrency permits. Keep exact content versions and independent original-page review notes. Bound loops and surface unresolved source gaps for human review.

An agent-reviewed candidate remains separate from formal human source approval and release. Follow registry_workflow.py for content-bound human signoff; keep all decisions immutable. No deployment, index rebuild, billing changes or messages to other chats are implied.

Current prerequisite status: all eleven records have scoped conversational acceptance. Begin the authorised expansion under the coordinator. Keep the separate page75 starting additions pending human review.

Agent 2 uses subagent_feedback.md as its feedback context and working prompt. Agents 1 and 3 also read its accepted lessons and rubric. Coordinator updates it, the review history and this progress marker at the end of every record-acceptance turn.


